   $q$What is the author's main purpose?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To explain how caterpillars turn into moths and butterflies.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"To describe an argument between two neighbors who dislike each other.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"To persuade readers to leave some fallen leaves in their yards.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To persuade readers to bag every leaf before winter begins.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-opposing-view"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To persuade readers to leave some fallen leaves in their yards.$q$, $q$The author explains the value of leaves and ends by saying a yard can be "neat and natural," which encourages readers to keep some leaves. Caterpillars are only one example of the creatures that use leaves.$q$, 'draft', '71a7b235-a699-57a7-b069-49186598661c')
