   $q$How has the author's own point of view about fallen leaves changed?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author once used a leaf blower but now uses a rake to save energy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The author once left every leaf but now bags them all because of Mr. Okafor.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-sequence"},{"text":"The author once bagged every leaf but now leaves many after learning their value.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The author has always left leaves and has never thought about bagging them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author once bagged every leaf but now leaves many after learning their value.$q$, $q$The author says, "I used to do the same thing," meaning bagging every leaf, and then says, "I now leave many of them where they land." Mr. Okafor's point changes how the author handles the lawn, not the author's overall view.$q$, 'draft', '71a7b235-a699-57a7-b069-49186598661c')
