   $q$What does Grandfather's choice to fold the tide chart into the speaker's hand suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He wants the speaker to use the chart as paper for drawing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"He is giving up the beach and will not return with the speaker.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He is scolding the speaker for not reading the chart that day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"He is passing on the skill of planning around the tide.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He is passing on the skill of planning around the tide.$q$, $q$The speaker promises to "draw faster" next time, and Grandfather laughs and hands over the chart that rules their trips, so he is sharing what he knows. His laugh shows he is not scolding.$q$, 'draft', 'd99e08b5-a05b-5f90-9ae2-5844bed4ada3')
