  ('c2720259-16b1-5c18-b862-e3e98ecf06ea', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-connections'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which statement best describes how the passage develops the idea that beavers can "reshape an entire landscape"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It compares beavers with other animals that build homes and shows which builder is strongest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-structure"},{"text":"It lists the complaints people have about beavers and explains why each complaint is wrong.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-purpose"},{"text":"It describes the steps a beaver follows to build a dam from the first stick to the last.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"It traces a chain of effects that starts with slower water and spreads to soil, plants, and animals.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It traces a chain of effects that starts with slower water and spreads to soil, plants, and animals.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 calls the pond the start of "a chain of other changes," and the next paragraphs follow that chain to soil, green land, and wildlife. The passage mentions dam building only briefly, so a step by step description is too narrow.$q$, 'draft', 'a9953528-1267-5f9f-995d-f8bac7ece0ad')
