   $q$How does Lindqvist's decision in paragraph 2 shape the events that follow?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By working alone on the first design, he finished quickly, which left more time for the summer festival.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"By building the mural from neighbors' memories, he gave them a stake in it, which drew them to help and gather.","is_correct":true},{"text":"By showing photos from overseas, he convinced the city to hold a festival in front of the new mural.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"By choosing a wall behind a laundromat, he made sure the owner would pay for every part of the project.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By building the mural from neighbors' memories, he gave them a stake in it, which drew them to help and gather.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 says he chose not to sketch a design himself and asked for neighbors' memories, and later they volunteer, paint, and point out "their own memories" at the wall. He did not work alone on the design, so the choice "By working alone on the first design, he finished quickly" contradicts the text.$q$, 'draft', '86b7274b-072c-5fea-95d6-ab4852445ebb')
