   $q$How does the example of fresh lettuce in January support the main idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that iceboxes worked better in winter, when the cold air kept the ice from melting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that grocery stores mattered less than farms once refrigerated trucks became common.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"It shows that families in cold cities grew lettuce indoors once they owned electric refrigerators.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"It shows that refrigeration changed not only homes but also how food travels from farms to people.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows that refrigeration changed not only homes but also how food travels from farms to people.$q$, $q$The lettuce example follows "Farming changed as well" and shows refrigerated trucks carrying food far without spoiling, which supports the closing idea that refrigeration reshaped how people "get their food." The lettuce was grown hundreds of miles away, not indoors.$q$, 'draft', '68c24f9b-c2a7-5495-b00a-1d18351220e2')
