   $q$Paragraph 5 says Keanu "was exhausted, yet he felt exhilarated." Using the contrast and the description that follows, what does "exhilarated" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"completely worn out","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-contrast"},{"text":"nervous about the next race","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"embarrassed by his finish","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"extremely happy and excited","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$extremely happy and excited$q$, $q$The word "yet" contrasts exhilarated with exhausted, and he feels like shouting across the park after his best finish, so it means very happy and excited. "Worn out" is what exhausted means, which the contrast rules out.$q$, 'draft', 'b5772e65-3b59-557f-87d0-d2c8c33f67f3')
