   $q$In paragraph 1, each new layer must "adhere" to the one beneath it. What does "adhere" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"to pull away from","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"to cool down on","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"to melt into","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-association"},{"text":"to stick to","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to stick to$q$, $q$The sentence restates the word as "sticking firmly so the object does not fall apart." The plastic is heated, but melting describes what happens before it is laid down, not what adhere means.$q$, 'draft', '5243e0d5-17a1-555c-a1fd-bf7701767dfa')
