  ('8b087f8a-e671-5ab8-a358-cfb83b895149', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-evidence-inference'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which pair of details together best supports the conclusion that the hive's temperature depends on cooperation rather than on one leader?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Beekeepers watch for signs of trouble, and a weak cluster may mean too little honey.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"No single bee is in charge of the temperature, and each worker responds to the conditions around her.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The bees form a cluster around their queen, and the queen stays in the warm center all winter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The hive stays near the same temperature, and the center of the nest is kept near 35 degrees.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-without-support"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$No single bee is in charge of the temperature, and each worker responds to the conditions around her.$q$, $q$The final paragraph directly says no bee is in charge and each worker reacts to her surroundings, which shows cooperation. The choice about the queen adds a claim the passage never makes, since it does not say the queen controls anything.$q$, 'draft', 'aeaf9011-fd97-5b0f-85cc-5efe2f2e41d8')
