  ('c4e520e2-9f56-5474-a625-3d7711759f30', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-evidence-inference'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which conclusion is best supported by the passage as a whole?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Lamplighters worked together to stop cities from switching over to electric streetlights.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Gas lamps were removed mainly because their leaks caused serious danger in most cities.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-evidence"},{"text":"Lamplighters did useful work their neighbors noticed, but central control of lighting made the job unnecessary.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Most towns today still rely on gas lamps and hire lamplighters to light them each night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Lamplighters did useful work their neighbors noticed, but central control of lighting made the job unnecessary.$q$, $q$The passage shows lamplighters cleaning, reporting problems and being known by residents, then explains that central switching ended their walks. Leaks are mentioned as one limit, but the text never says they were the main reason lamps were removed.$q$, 'draft', '5a0745b1-5ec2-5359-a0f2-84878d4b04ea')
