   $q$The passage ends by saying "What has changed is how people understand the effects of that behavior." Which evidence best supports this statement?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Frogs lay their eggs in calm pond water, and ducks and herons feed along the edges of the pond.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Dams can flood roads and farm fields, and beavers chew through trees that landowners want to keep.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A family of beavers can cut down small trees and build a dam that slows the water in a stream.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"describes-behavior-not-change"},{"text":"People once saw dams mostly as a nuisance, but scientists now see benefits like stored water and wildlife homes.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$People once saw dams mostly as a nuisance, but scientists now see benefits like stored water and wildlife homes.$q$, $q$The statement is about a change in understanding, so the best evidence shows both the old view and the new one. The flooding detail shows only the old view, so by itself it cannot show that anything changed.$q$, 'draft', '0f15e3de-08ef-5e31-bf53-4231f29ae673')
