   $q$Based on the passage, what can the reader infer about the teammates who "peel away" near the finish?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They used up their own energy at the front so a sheltered teammate could sprint to win.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They never drafted during the race, so they were too tired to keep riding hard.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They are the fastest sprinters on the team and are saving their speed for later.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They leave the group near the finish mainly to avoid crashing in a crowded sprint.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They used up their own energy at the front so a sheltered teammate could sprint to win.$q$, $q$Paragraph 4 says these teammates "have done the hard work at the front" while the sheltered rider saved energy, so they spent their strength helping her. The crash risk is real, but the text links peeling away to the team's strategy, not to safety.$q$, 'draft', 'b282c102-d8f5-538b-9475-b9d1ae229035')
