-- Passage rg7-evidence-inference-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('204357be-c358-55cb-b4df-43a765818cdb', 'rg7-evidence-inference-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-evidence-inference'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Our Lunch Scraps Could Feed Our Garden$q$, $q$Every day after lunch, the trash cans in our cafeteria fill with apple cores, banana peels and half-eaten sandwiches. All of it goes to a landfill. I believe our school should start a compost program, and I think the evidence shows it would be worth the effort.

First, food scraps make up a large share of what we throw away. Last month, the student council sorted one day's cafeteria trash. By weight, more than half of it was food. Paper napkins and trays made up most of the rest. Only a small amount was plastic.

Second, composting turns waste into something useful. When food scraps break down with leaves and soil, they become a dark, rich material that helps plants grow. Our school already has a vegetable garden behind the science wing. Right now, the garden club buys bags of compost every spring. With our own compost, the club could spend that money on seeds and tools instead.

Some people worry that compost bins will smell or attract pests. These are fair concerns. However, a covered bin that is turned regularly and mixed with dry leaves usually stays clean. Two nearby elementary schools have run compost programs for years without these problems.

Finally, a compost program would teach us something. Students would learn how decomposition works by watching it happen. They would also see how much food they waste, which might encourage them to take only what they will eat.

Starting this program would require a few bins, clear signs and student volunteers to sort scraps. The council has already found twelve volunteers. I hope the principal will give us the chance to try it for one semester.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
