  ('54a8d16c-2d64-512a-a454-04f09eb20714', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In the last paragraph, the author says that with an allusion, "a whole story is packed into just a few words." What does the author mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Writers should shorten old stories so that readers can finish them faster.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"A short phrase can bring the meaning of a longer, familiar story to mind.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Allusions are confusing because they leave out most of the important details.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The myths in the passage were first written on very small pieces of paper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A short phrase can bring the meaning of a longer, familiar story to mind.$q$, $q$An allusion "refer[s] to a well-known story," so a few words like "Midas touch" call up the whole tale and its lesson. The author is not suggesting that stories should be shortened; "packed" is a metaphor for how much meaning a phrase carries.$q$, 'draft', 'ce88d1e3-6a8b-5f40-ad46-7c5d0d7a5d8d')
