   $q$Grandpa says the clock "has been asleep for twenty years." What does he mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The clock rings an alarm to wake people up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The clock runs very slowly but still ticks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The clock has not worked for twenty years.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The clock was made exactly twenty years ago.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The clock has not worked for twenty years.$q$, $q$Clocks cannot sleep, so the phrase means the clock has been stopped, and later it "began to tick" again once it was fixed. A clock that still ticks would not need to be woken up.$q$, 'draft', 'd65270b0-2b8f-5ced-95de-c4c1fd0ad78c')
