  ('d0843214-a29b-52c0-97ec-cf1a75691250', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Grandpa says, "A clock is like a team." What idea does this analogy explain?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Fixing clocks is a sport that people compete in to win prizes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Each part relies on the others, so one failing part stops the whole.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Clocks work best when several people repair them at the same time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-analogy"},{"text":"Every clock has one main gear that controls all of the others.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Each part relies on the others, so one failing part stops the whole.$q$, $q$Grandpa explains, "Every gear depends on the gear next to it," just as teammates depend on each other. The analogy compares the gears to a team; it does not say a clock needs several repairers.$q$, 'draft', 'd65270b0-2b8f-5ced-95de-c4c1fd0ad78c')
