   $q$Some bridges have machines that work "like a giant hair dryer that never shuts off." What does this simile tell the reader?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The machines heat the steel cables until they become soft.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The machines blow dry air through the cables all the time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The machines turn on only once a year for a quick check.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Bridge workers dry their hair after climbing in the rain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The machines blow dry air through the cables all the time.$q$, $q$The text says the machines "blow dry air through the cables," and "never shuts off" shows they run constantly. Running once a year is the opposite of never shutting off.$q$, 'draft', 'dd2590a3-c0e6-5a34-89a6-fa7468410075')
