   $q$Elijah says the later start would make the school day "a million years long." What kind of language is this?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A comparison of the school day to an animal","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-figure-of-speech"},{"text":"A quiet statement that makes the change seem small","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"An exaggeration to make the day sound much too long","is_correct":true},{"text":"An exact fact about how long the school day lasts","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An exaggeration to make the day sound much too long$q$, $q$"A million years" is hyperbole, a huge exaggeration, since the day would end "only fifteen minutes later." It is not a fact, which is exactly why Soo-ah can correct it.$q$, 'draft', 'a13b98dc-7e03-5ab6-8a07-82bb3be47390')
