   $q$The muffins "disappeared faster than snow in July." What does this comparison mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The muffins were left uneaten for many hours.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"The bakery forgot to deliver the muffins.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The volunteers ate the muffins very quickly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The muffins melted in the hot summer sun.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The volunteers ate the muffins very quickly.$q$, $q$Snow would vanish almost instantly in July, so the comparison exaggerates how fast the muffins were eaten. The muffins did not actually melt; the snow is only the thing they are compared to.$q$, 'draft', '756a1566-b585-55bb-ad40-7a1ea1811c87')
