   $q$What does the repeated line "Up the keys and down again" show about the speaker's practice?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker is learning a brand new song every single day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The speaker plays the same scales over and over each day.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The speaker is moving the piano up and down the stairs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The speaker refuses to practice and walks away from the piano.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker plays the same scales over and over each day.$q$, $q$Like the practice itself, the line repeats in each stanza, showing the same scales played again and again. The poem is about scales, not about learning new songs.$q$, 'draft', '87aa5ec6-ebf2-5a87-b76e-6e1b04448789')
