   $q$Why does the final stanza leave out the repeated line and become longer than the others?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows the week is over, so the speaker no longer has to practice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"It shows the speaker has grown bored of piano and wants to quit.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"It shows the brother is now the one speaking in the poem.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-speaker"},{"text":"It shows practice no longer feels like repetition, because playing comes naturally.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows practice no longer feels like repetition, because playing comes naturally.$q$, $q$Dropping the refrain mirrors the speaker no longer counting and repeating; the music "simply carries" them. The speaker sounds happy and confident, not bored, so quitting does not fit.$q$, 'draft', '87aa5ec6-ebf2-5a87-b76e-6e1b04448789')
