  ('a7af6f1a-178d-5ab1-ab2b-93413b6401c7', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Why does the author place Grandma Ines's section between Mateo's two sections?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The reader learns her plan first, so Mateo's last section shows it working.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It proves that Mateo was right to think the garden trip was pointless.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"It interrupts the story so the reader forgets about the beans for a while.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-craft"},{"text":"It shows that Grandma's memories of the hillside matter more than Mateo.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The reader learns her plan first, so Mateo's last section shows it working.$q$, $q$Because Grandma predicts that Mateo will ask why the beans failed, the reader recognizes her plan succeeding when he does ask and then reads the packet. The ending shows Mateo becoming curious, so the trip was not pointless.$q$, 'draft', '54757fb5-2297-5585-970f-f9c0d88d28be')
