   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Gas lamps were installed in the 1800s and replaced in the 1900s. Today, a few towns still keep gas lamps on their historic streets for visitors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"omits-central-idea"},{"text":"Lamplighters had one of the hardest and most admirable jobs in history. It is sad that electric lights put these hardworking people out of work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Lamplighters carried long poles with a flame or hook at the end. In the morning they cleaned soot off the glass and reported any broken lamps.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"In the 1800s, lamplighters lit and cared for gas streetlamps every day, which let city life continue after dark. Electric lights later made the job unnecessary.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In the 1800s, lamplighters lit and cared for gas streetlamps every day, which let city life continue after dark. Electric lights later made the job unnecessary.$q$, $q$The summary that begins "In the 1800s, lamplighters lit and cared for" includes the job, its effect on cities and its end, with no opinions. The summary calling the job "most admirable" adds judgments like "most admirable" and "sad," which an objective summary leaves out.$q$, 'draft', '8de43da8-d691-511e-b6e3-fcd4fe8b1c04')
