   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Beavers cause floods on roads and farm fields and cut down trees people want. Because of this, most communities now remove beavers from their land.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Beavers are slow on land but strong swimmers. They build lodges in the middle of their ponds, and the lodges have underwater entrances that keep predators away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Beavers are amazing animals, and people should never complain about them. Flooded roads are a small price to pay for all the good that beavers do.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Beavers build dams that turn streams into ponds. These ponds shelter many animals, keep soil moist, reduce flooding and clean water, though dams can sometimes cause problems for people.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Beavers build dams that turn streams into ponds. These ponds shelter many animals, keep soil moist, reduce flooding and clean water, though dams can sometimes cause problems for people.$q$, $q$The summary that begins "Beavers build dams that turn streams into ponds" covers the dams, the benefits and the problems without adding opinions. The summary saying most communities now remove beavers contradicts paragraph 5, which says some communities install pipes instead of removing beavers.$q$, 'draft', 'ab3b0170-94ff-5ade-beab-b854dcc8f156')
