   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Noise-canceling headphones are the best invention for travelers. Anyone who rides a bus or airplane should buy a pair before the next trip.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Noise-canceling headphones block every kind of sound completely. Their microphones and padded ear cups keep out engines, voices and barking dogs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Noise-canceling headphones use microphones and a chip to make sound waves opposite to steady noise, so the waves cancel. Padding helps block sudden sounds the electronics miss.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sound is made of waves of pressure that have high and low points. Our ears notice these changes in pressure and send signals to the brain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Noise-canceling headphones use microphones and a chip to make sound waves opposite to steady noise, so the waves cancel. Padding helps block sudden sounds the electronics miss.$q$, $q$The summary about making opposite sound waves and adding padding explains the cancellation and the role of padding without opinions. The summary claiming the headphones block every kind of sound contradicts paragraph 5, which says some sudden noise still gets through.$q$, 'draft', '57630e0b-aecf-53bc-a0c0-e360656fc581')
