  ('0728b64f-95cf-5979-a644-7f7a56443363', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-main-idea-summary'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A student summarized the passage this way: "Headphones use microphones to record sounds and then play them back louder." What is the main problem with this summary?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It misstates the key idea, since the headphones create an opposite wave to cancel noise.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It includes the writer's personal opinion about how useful the headphones are.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-error"},{"text":"It leaves out the fact that sound travels as waves through the air.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"It focuses too much on padded ear cups instead of the electronic parts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-error"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It misstates the key idea, since the headphones create an opposite wave to cancel noise.$q$, $q$Paragraph 3 says the chip makes a wave that is "the exact opposite of the noise," not a louder copy, so the summary gets the central process wrong. Leaving out the sound wave background is a small gap, but the larger problem is the inaccurate main idea.$q$, 'draft', '57630e0b-aecf-53bc-a0c0-e360656fc581')
