   $q$What is the author's central claim in this opinion piece?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Middle schools should require cooking because it is a valuable life skill.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Students should learn chemistry by watching bread rise in the oven.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Fast food contains too much salt, sugar and fat for growing teens.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Schools do not have enough money to pay for new classes or kitchens.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-counterclaim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Middle schools should require cooking because it is a valuable life skill.$q$, $q$The last sentence of paragraph 1 states the claim directly, and every later paragraph supports it. The point about money is a counterargument the author answers, not the author's own claim.$q$, 'draft', '936e37eb-2b76-5e44-b323-e6ee4d0af433')
